              "description": "Identifies `gitsync sync` and `gitsync run`, which force-push and prune every configured repo's branches and tags to GitHub so the two sides end up identical, and can eventually delete the GitHub mirror once a repo disappears from the source (subject to gitsync's own delete_grace and delete_limit safeguards). Both accept --help/-h, and `run` also accepts --dry-run, but gitsync's flag parser (Go's stdlib flag.FlagSet) stops at the first token that isn't a flag and never looks at anything after it - so a flag placed after a repo name, or after any other token, is silently ignored and the command still runs live. No safe variant is reliable against that, so this rule always reviews sync and run regardless of which flags are present.",
              "family": null,
              "matcher": {
                "config": {},
                "matchers": [
                  {
                    "config": {
                      "allow_leading_options": true,
                      "executables": [
                        "gitsync",
                        "gitsync.exe"
